   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the disqualification of bus drivers",
    "basePrintNo": "S5806",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5806-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §509-cc, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5806               REVISED 08/17/11\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the\ndisqualification of bus drivers\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo prohibit individuals who are convicted of certain offenses\ninvolving children from being school bus drivers.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1: Amends Subdivision 4 of section 509-cc of the vehicle and\ntraffic law to include convictions under the following sections of\nthe penal law among those which would result in permanent\ndisqualification from being a school bus driver:\n\n*Section 120.12 - Aggravated assault upon a person less than 11\nyears old\n*Section 120.70 - Luring a child\n*Section 125.11 - Aggravated criminally negligent homicide\n*Section 125.13 - Vehicular manslaughter in the first degree\n*Section 125.14 - Aggravated vehicular homicide\n*Section 125.15 - Manslaughter in the second degree\n*Section 125.21 - Aggravated manslaughter in the second degree\n*Section 125.22 - Aggravated manslaughter in the first degree\n*Section 130.53 - Persistent sexual abuse\n*Section 130.65-a - Aggravated sexual abuse in the fourth degree\n*Section 130.66 - Aggravated sexual abuse in the third degree\n*Section 130.67 - Aggravated sexual abuse in the second degree\n*Section 130.75 - Course of sexual conduct against a child in\nthe first degree\n*Section 130.80 - Course of sexual conduct against a childin\nthe second degree\n*Section 130.90 - Facilitating a sex offense with a controlled\nsubstance\n*Section 130.95 - Predatory sexual assault\n*Section 130.96 - Predatory sexual assault against a child\n*Section 220.44 - Criminal sale of a controlled substance in\nor near school grounds\n*Section 230.25 - Promoting prostitution in the third degree\n*Section 230.30 - Promoting prostitution in the second degree\n*Section 230.32 - Promoting prostitution in the first degree\n*Section 230.34 - Sex trafficking\n*Section 235.22 - Disseminating indecent material to\nminors in the first degree\n*Section 263.05 - Use of a child in a sexual performance\n*Section 263.10 - Promoting an obscene sexual performance by a child\n*Section 263.11 - Possessing an obscene sexual performance by a child\n*Section 263.15 - Promoting a sexual performance by a child\n*Section 263.16 - Possessing a sexual performance by a child\n\nIt also adds convictions under the following sections of the penal law\namong those which would result in disqualification for a period of\nfive years:\n\n\n*Section 130.52 - Forcible touching\n*Section 220.65 - Criminal sale of a prescription for a controlled\nsubstance\n\nSection 2: Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nCurrent law includes a number of offenses which permanently disqualify\nan individual from being a school bus driver, this legislation\nupdates the law by including offenses involving children that were\ndeveloped after this original law was enacted.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall have become a law. Effective immediately the adoption of any\nrules or regulations necessary for the timely implementation of the\nprovisions of this act are authorized to be made on or before such\neffective date.\n\n",
